From 3210007ae449abebb12a8edd0262754e6cc9ecbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:59:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] win32pbs: bridge images between the Windows clipboard
 and gpbs

gpbs only passed text (CF_UNICODETEXT) between the Windows clipboard and
the general pasteboard, so an image copied in a Windows program could not
be pasted into a GNUstep app, nor the reverse.

Windows to GNUstep: when the clipboard holds a DIB, a bitmap (which
Windows turns into a DIB) or a "PNG", NSTIFFPboardType is declared, and
NSPasteboardTypePNG as well for a PNG.  The data is made when asked for:
a PNG is passed through or converted to TIFF; otherwise the CF_DIB is
converted, 32 bit DIBs directly and other depths and compressions
through GDI.  CF_DIB is read rather than CF_DIBV5, as the CF_DIBV5
Windows synthesizes can carry colour masks after its header.

GNUstep to Windows: when the general pasteboard holds TIFF or PNG, CF_DIB
(32 bit, alpha in the fourth byte) and "PNG" are published with delayed
rendering, as the text is.  WM_RENDERFORMAT now renders the format it
is asked for, WM_RENDERALLFORMATS renders the image formats too, and
CF_UNICODETEXT is only published when the pasteboard holds a string.

Tests/win32/pasteboard.m checks both directions for images and text.

This change was written with the help of an AI assistant (Claude); the
code was reviewed and tested by the author before submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
